-- title:
--   Each restart stage has at most tau warm occupation budgets in expectation
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$ with $n>0$. Let $M_1,M_2$ be matroids on $[n]$ whose ground sets are all of $[n]$ and whose ranks both equal $r$, and let $o_1,o_2$ be their exact independence oracles. Let $p=(\varepsilon,\delta)$ have rational $0<\varepsilon,\delta<1$, and let $s$ be the constructed annealing schedule, with $L$ phases, ratio $\rho$, $N$ observations per phase, $\tau$ return transitions per restart stage, draw cap $T$, and shared restart-attempt cap $A$. Let $B$ be the prescribed random block length. A good stored table means that, at every stored level $a\le j$, each multiplier lies between one quarter and four times the ratio of the transversal partition sum to its defect-class partition sum at $\rho^a$; the current multipliers obey the same condition at level $j$. A certified phase is an actual successful phase update with good input tables and good next-phase tables when they will be used, whose product multiplier approximates the true successive transversal-partition ratio within factors $(1-\eta)/(1+\eta)$ and $(1+\eta)/(1-\eta)$, where $\eta=s.\eta$. Fix $j<L$, a Boolean prefix $h$, and a restart-prefix witness: a length-$B$ Boolean word with all earlier phases certified, reaching a cursor $v$ before phase $j$, with good stored tables, and $h$ equal to that word truncated at $v.\mathrm{bitCursor}$. Set $t=B-|h|$. Fix $i<j$ and assume $\rho^{i+1}>0$ and positivity of every entry of the stored table $v.\mathrm{tables}(i+1)$. Let $\pi$ be the normalized operational law at these parameters, let $P$ be its ideal lazy exchange Metropolis chain, and let $\mathcal T$ be the transversal states. For a finite chain $P$ and target set $\mathcal T$, define survival probabilities by $$S_0(x)=\mathbf1_{x\notin\mathcal T},\qquad S_{m+1}(x)=\mathbf1_{x\notin\mathcal T}\sum_yP(x,y)S_m(y).$$ Put $H_0(x)=1$ and $H_{m+1}(x)=\sum_yP(x,y)S_m(y)$. For a distribution $\pi$, the finite return occupation is $$O_H(P,\mathcal T,\pi)=\pi(\mathcal T)+\sum_{m=0}^{H-1}\sum_{x\in\mathcal T}\pi(x)\sum_yP(x,y)S_m(y).$$ On a suffix $b\in\{0,1\}^t$, let $C_i(b)$ be the sum of the attempted chain transitions in the $\tau$ return calls of stage $i$, starting from their actual stopped cursors after the fresh transversal and previous stages; absent cursors contribute zero and attempts ending in abort are included. Then $$2^{-t}\sum_b C_i(b)\le\tau\,\frac4{\pi(\mathcal T)}\,O_A(P,\mathcal T,\pi).$$
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/RestartStageAttemptMean.lean#L170-L319

